It seems to me that despite potential bias you'd want to use Elevation to account for varying detection probabilities (assuming that's an appropriate factor for the detection part of the model).  That's what Community N-Mixture multinomial models are for:  getting more appropriate estimates of population size.  I would use the caveat that doing so has not yet been fully investigated when using those adjusted counts for subsequent analyses.

But certainly a more appropriate/complete analysis would include the subsequent analyses in a complete model.  That sounds like an opportunity to write more publications and code.

Jim

